<title>BELARUS: BELARUS SIGNS 120,000 T S.AFRICAN SUGAR CONTRACT.</title>
<headline>BELARUS SIGNS 120,000 T S.AFRICAN SUGAR CONTRACT.</headline>
<dateline>MINSK 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The former Soviet republic of Belarus plans to buy 200,000 tonnes of raw sugar from Cuba and Latin America, Agriculture Minister Vasily Leonov told Reuters on Friday.</p>
<p>He said that a contract had also been signed for 120,000 tonnes of raws for delivery from South Africa, but gave no details on delivery dates or prices.</p>
<p>Leonov said Belarus had imposed a 35 percent value-added tax on refined sugar imports.   </p>
<p>The value-added tax would mostly affect neighbouring Ukraine, a traditional exporter to Belarus, he said.</p>
<p>Leonov said Belarus expected to harvest 1.1 million tonnes of sugar beet this year, the same as last year, and would produce 120,000 tonnes of refined sugar.</p>
<p>Russia imposed a 10 percent VAT on all Ukrainian raw and refined sugar imports at the beginning of the month.</p>
<p>-- Kiev newsroom +380 44 229 2264</p>
